Requirements
Requirement	Module	Access program	Statement
tools.1	tools	serve	The tools MUST give the access program serve of the server as their own.
read.2	read	read	A pathname at or within the folder the data bank's access program folder gives MUST be answered by the data bank: the folder by its names, an input's file, the _file of its record of _inputs, by its records, then their records of _stored, and any other pathname within it refused, never by reading its files.
read.4	read	read	The data bank's folder read with a selection or a filter MUST be answered by the records of every input, a sheet of one name in several inputs given as the union of their records, each record led by its _input.
read.6	read	read	A pathname, a file, a selection or a filter refused MUST end the read as refused, with its reason.
read.7	read	read	Every other pathname MUST be read as the files read › input's members names, each by conversion's sheets, the sheets of every file chosen by the relational model's chosen, and the reply given by reply.
read.8	read	read	A file of a directory whose conversion ends as no format or failed MUST be named in not read, its status that error's name and its reason that error's reason, and the read go on.
read.10	read	read	A file named directly whose conversion ends as no format or failed MUST end the read as refused, its reason that error's name, then, for failed, a colon, a space and that error's reason.
read.9	read	read	What a file's conversion leaves behind MUST be named in left behind, one record for each thing, in order.
read-input.1	read › input	members	The pathname MUST be absolute.
read-input.5	read › input	members	A pathname that is not absolute MUST be refused as not absolute.
read-input.2	read › input	members	A pathname naming a directory MUST name each regular file in it whose name does not begin with a dot, in the order of their names' code points, the directories within it not read, and each other entry named in not read as skipped.
read-input.3	read › input	members	A pathname that names neither a directory nor a regular file, a directory that cannot be listed, and a file named directly that cannot be read MUST be refused with the reason: names neither a directory nor a regular file, cannot be listed, or cannot be read.
read-input.4	read › input	members	The same file reached by two pathnames MUST be one file, named by its resolved pathname.
conversion.1	conversion	sheets	A file whose name ends .mtsv MUST be read by the parser.
conversion.2	conversion	sheets	A file whose extension names a format MUST be read by that format's module: .csv by csv, .json by json, .xlsx by xlsx and .ods by ods, each from the nodes package reads, and .sqlite by sqlite.
conversion.3	conversion	sheets	What a file holds that MTSV does not MUST be left behind, each thing named as its format's module names it, in order.
conversion.4	conversion	sheets	A file whose extension names no format MUST end its conversion as no format; one that cannot be read, as failed, its reason cannot be read; and one whose conversion ends with an error, as failed, its reason that error's name.
package.1	package	nodes	A zip entry MUST be read stored or deflated, the compression methods its package's format allows.
package.4	package	nodes	A zip entry compressed otherwise MUST end the read of its package as compression method not allowed.
package.2	package	nodes	Each entry of a package whose name ends .xml or .rels MUST be read as XML into the relation nodes, each element, attribute and run of character data one node, each name expanded with its namespace, a namespace declaration being no node.
package.3	package	nodes	A package that is not a zip file, or an entry it reads as XML that is not well-formed, MUST end the read of its package as failed.
csv.1	csv	load	csv MUST read a CSV file, its octets UTF-8, as one sheet whose sheet name is empty, its first record the header.
csv.2	csv	load	A field that MTSV cannot hold, or a sheet name holding HT, LF, FF or CR, MUST end the load as cannot be represented.
json.1	json	load	json MUST read a JSON file, through JSON text, as sheets: its value an array of objects, each with the members sheet name, header and records, one sheet each.
json.2	json	load	A value that is not a string, or a field that MTSV cannot hold, or a sheet name holding HT, LF, FF or CR, MUST end the load as cannot be represented.
xlsx.1	xlsx	load	xlsx MUST read each worksheet of a workbook as one sheet, named as the worksheet, each cell's value as its text, and leave behind every type, formula and style a cell holds, each named by the cell's reference, a space, and its name in the cell: t, f or s.
xlsx.2	xlsx	load	A cell's text that MTSV cannot hold, or a sheet name holding HT, LF, FF or CR, MUST end the load as cannot be represented.
xlsx.3	xlsx	load	A workbook whose part a relationship it reads names is not among its nodes MUST end the load as failed.
ods.1	ods	load	ods MUST read each table of a spreadsheet document as one sheet, named as the table, each cell's text as its value, and leave behind every type, formula and style a cell holds, each named by the cell's reference in A1 style, a space, and its attribute's name: office:value-type and the value attribute it selects, table:formula or table:style-name.
ods.2	ods	load	A cell's text that MTSV cannot hold, or a sheet name holding HT, LF, FF or CR, MUST end the load as cannot be represented.
ods.3	ods	load	A spreadsheet document whose nodes hold no part content.xml, or whose body holds no office:spreadsheet, MUST end the load as failed.
sqlite.1	sqlite	load	sqlite MUST read each table of a database as one sheet, named as the table, its column names the header, each value the text CAST AS TEXT gives it and a NULL an empty field, and leave behind views, indexes, triggers and the objects whose names begin with sqlite_, each named by its type, a space, and its name, as sqlite_schema holds them.
sqlite.2	sqlite	load	A value whose typeof is blob, or a field that MTSV cannot hold, or a sheet name holding HT, LF, FF or CR, MUST end the load as cannot be represented.
sqlite.3	sqlite	load	A file that does not begin with the database header's magic string MUST end the load as failed.
reply.5	reply	reply	Every reply MUST be the report, then, with a pathname alone, the map, and with a selection, the values chosen.
reply.1	reply	reply	The report MUST be the sheets file, not read, left behind and sheets, in that order, each with its header even when it holds no record.
reply.2	reply	reply	The map MUST be the sheet fields: the name of each field of each sheet chosen.
reply.3	reply	reply	The reply MUST be written by the generator.
server.1	server	serve	The server MUST speak MCP over the stdio transport, reading its standard input and writing its standard output, until its standard input ends.
server.2	server	serve	The server MUST answer server/discover with its name the Value server name, its version the Value version, and its instructions the Value server instructions with {data bank folder} filled with the folder the data bank's access program folder gives.
server.3	server	serve	The server MUST offer one tool, named by the Value tool name and described by the Value tool description, whose input schema is an object whose properties are the arguments tool arguments names, each a string named as the parameter of read's read it is handed as, those tool arguments marks required its required properties.
server.6	server	serve	An argument the tool is not given MUST be handed to read as the empty text.
server.4	server	serve	The tool's result MUST be one text content holding the reply, and no structured content.
server.5	server	serve	A call refused, or ended as keeping failed, MUST be reported as a tool execution error whose text is the reason.
